==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*þwahaną}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|thwahan|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|dwahan|lang=goh}}, Old Norse {{term|þvá|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌸𐍅𐌰𐌷𐌰𐌽|tr=þwahan|lang=got}}. The Germanic base is also the source of English {{term|towel|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/θwæːan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=þwēan}}

# to [[wash]], [[anoint]]

